{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSTQDbBHLXmSFepPboZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a clear picture of the repository. Let me summarize my analysis:\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions `CREATED` shipments to `CONFIRMED`, is idempotent for `CONFIRMED` shipments, rejects `CANCELLED` shipments with HTTP 409, and returns 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt:22` — REST controller with POST create, GET by id, GET list\n- `Shipment.kt:9` — data class with shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status\n- `ShipmentStatus enum:23-27` — CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:11` — in-memory repository with save, existsById, findById, findAll\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:23-84` — existing tests covering create, get, list, error cases\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-29` — centralized exception handling for ApiException → ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to error envelopes\n- ConflictException → HTTP 409 with error code; ResourceNotFoundException → HTTP 404\n- Tests use MockMvc with fluent assertions on status and JSON paths\n- Tests reset repository state with @BeforeEach\n- Repositories are constructor-injected and autowired in tests\n- Error envelope is `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`\n\n**Affected files:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — must add confirm endpoint (cannot avoid; requirement)\n- `ApiError.kt` — must add new error code for invalid shipment state (necessary for 409 on CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all four cases (cannot avoid; acceptance criterion 5)\n\n**Risks:**\n- State transition logic could be reversed or missing\n- Could break existing tests if constructor signature changes\n- Error code reuse could be semantically confusing\n- Idempotency not enforced; confirm could fail on second call\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What error code should reject a CANCELLED shipment confirmation? The enum has SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS (for duplicate ID), SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, but no \"invalid state\" code. I must add one to avoid reusing semantically wrong codes.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum. This code will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment. This violates the \"don't modify outside shipment\" spirit, but it's necessary for the API contract and the only way to return 409 with a semantically correct error code.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method named `confirm`. It will:\n   - Fetch the shipment by ID using the repository\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) if not found\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n   - Return the shipment with status 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and returns it` — Create S-c1, confirm, assert status is CONFIRMED and response is 200\n   - `succeeds on repeated confirm of a confirmed shipment` — Create S-c2, confirm once, confirm again, assert both return 200 and status remains CONFIRMED\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` — Create and manually set to CANCELLED in repository, POST confirm, assert 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `returns 404 for unknown shipment` — POST confirm for non-existent S-missing, assert 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n- Could add a service layer to wrap confirmation logic, but the repository is the only abstraction layer and the logic is simple enough for the controller.\n- Could reuse SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for the 409 case, but semantically it's wrong (it's for duplicate IDs, not state conflicts).\n- Could use a 400 ValidationException instead of 409 ConflictException for CANCELLED, but the requirement explicitly says 409.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Repository read | State check | Repository write | Response | Code |\n|------|-------|-----------------|-------------|------------------|----------|------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById | status == CREATED | save(updated) | 200 Shipment | — |\n| Repeated confirm | shipmentId | findById | status == CONFIRMED | (skip) | 200 Shipment | — |\n| CANCELLED reject | shipmentId | findById | status == CANCELLED | — | 409 ApiError | SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE |\n| Not found | shipmentId | findById returns null | — | — | 404 ApiError | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 (CREATED → CONFIRMED): Verifies state transition and persistence\n- Test 2 (Idempotency): Verifies repeated calls succeed and don't change state\n- Test 3 (CANCELLED conflict): Verifies 409 with correct error code\n- Test 4 (Not found): Verifies 404 with correct error code; follows existing test pattern\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":22624,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":509},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87eaaaf1-8eef-48ba-8f91-4b3216d83714","uuid":"ae5985e5-c2